s5-2-p15 : Block
s5-2-p15 = prose (cons "**Reusing a theorem.** A proved statement is a dependent function from its assumptions to its conclusion. If a library theorem has type \(h:\prod_{a:A}P(a)\to Q(a)\), importing it into another construction consists of supplying \(a:A\) and \(p:P(a)\), then applying \(h(a,p):Q(a)\). The assumptions are retained in the type. A change of representation uses the previously defined transport operation on the complete dependent construction; there is no separate shortcut that discards hypotheses." nil)
